it's quieter than usual on Barley's  beaches tens of thousands of Chinese  tourists who would have spent their  winter holidays on the island have had  to postpone their plans because of the  corona virus outbreak for visitors from  China who landed here before the  outbreak escalated there are two choices  return home or extend their stay at  least 300 out of the 5,000 who are here  have applied for visa extensions but Yan  Dongsheng and her husband are ready to  go home the couple say they're confident  Chinese authorities and governments  around the world are handling the  situation we need to go back to our jobs  and our children need to go to school so  in our holiday ants we will immediately  return home every year around a million  Chinese tourists visit Bali and there  were direct flights from Wuhan where the  outbreak began until they were stopped a  few weeks ago as many asked how  Indonesia has seemingly avoided this  outbreak for now there's concern the  virus is present here but undetected  somewhere in this vast archipelago a  recent study by Harvard researchers  looked at data around the outbreak and  its link with air travel volume it  calculated the risk of an outbreak in  countries with direct flights to Wuhan  when the outbreak began and found the  disease could already be in Indonesia  some say Indonesia is vulnerable did not  mean a dirty but what you need to look  there are many ports of entry into the  country so many airports and ways for  people to get in and some rural areas  don't have the right equipment to detect  to the virus  but authorities here are defending  measures taken by Indonesia we've been  mapping the spread of what would happen  if there was an outbreak we have 100  hospitals ready now and more are getting  ready the facilities and personnel are  prepared the World Health Organization  also says the country is taking the  right steps to detect the virus and  prepare for cases we are fully confident  the Indonesians National Lab has the  test and they are competent to detect  any transmission it's been confirmed one  Chinese national who traveled to Bali  has contracted the virus but it's not  clear whether that happened in Bali or  elsewhere authorities are looking into  the case and on this island  many are anxiously waiting to know  Jessica Washington al Jazeera Bali
 

